<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalyan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalyan is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thane">Thane</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the Ulhas river north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Mumbai</a>. In antiquity it was a port linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> with western trade, mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/periplus-of-the-erythraean-sea">Periplus of the Erythraean Sea</a> and in donors' inscriptions in the Kanheri and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nashik">Nashik</a> caves. It remained an important port and town under later dynasties and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kalyan.jpg" alt="Kalyan" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Udaykumar PR · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalyan_Railway_Yard,_Kalyan,_Maharashtra,_India_-_panoramio_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
